#---
# purpose: "fz-kdt.198 — a bare inner is rejected at a brand-typed @spec position"
# expect: diagnostic
# diagnostic.code: spec/violation
#---
#
# # brand_rejects_a_bare_inner
#
# The other half of the refinement law. `Utf8.to_bytes/1` declares `@spec
# to_bytes(utf8) :: binary`; a raw byte literal has not been through
# `Utf8.from_bytes!/1`, so it carries no tag and the call is a `spec/violation`
# on every path. Nothing at runtime could tell the two values apart — this is a
# TYPING verdict, which is exactly why the brand axis has to be brand-aware
# while equality stays brand-blind.
fn main() do
  dbg(Utf8.to_bytes(<<104, 105>>))
end
